    {
      "id": "scale",
      "label": "Scale",
      "description": "The actor empty's Blender scale, exported as 'scale' [x, y, z, 1] (game axes) whenever it isn't 1. Options: \"always\": true writes it even at 1 (citb-plat crashes without it); \"uniform\": true for actors that read one float (eco-door, orbit-plat, sharkey: X is used). On the process-drawable root, so any actor exports its scale (e.g. for a process-drawable scale hack); vanilla code reads it in citb-plat, eco-door, orbit-plat, sharkey.",
      "fields": []
    },
    {"id": "custom-fields", "label": "Actor Settings", "description": "Generic per-actor fields, written out in full in the actor's entry.", "fields": []},
